# What the Docker daemon must never send into a build context.
# The image is built from the repository root, so everything here is an
# exclusion from a context that would otherwise contain real credentials.
#
# Patterns are matched by Docker with Go's filepath.Match rules: a pattern with
# no interior "/" is anchored at the context root and matches nothing deeper,
# while "**/" spans any number of directories. Anything that exists only in
# subdirectories (caches, egg-info) therefore needs the "**/" form, or
# `COPY src/ ./src/` would bake it into the image.
.env
.env.*
.venv/
.git/
data/
*.db
*.log
cookies.txt
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.review/
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/
